WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.843 --> 00:00:17.725
Jason walked slowly into the kitchen behind his friends.

2
00:00:17.745 --> 00:00:22.749
"We're making oven-fried chicken today," Chef said.

3
00:00:22.769 --> 00:00:27.153
"Yum! Could we have a picnic outside?"

4
00:00:27.573 --> 00:00:28.194
Izzie said.

5
00:00:28.214 --> 00:00:35.247
"Okay. Just behave yourselves and pay attention," Chef said sternly.

6
00:00:37.009 --> 00:00:38.770
Everyone cheered except for Jason.

7
00:00:41.312 --> 00:00:42.954
He crossed his arms and frowned.

8
00:00:42.974 --> 00:00:46.377
"What's wrong?

9
00:00:47.518 --> 00:00:50.180
You're as grumpy as Chef!"

10
00:00:50.580 --> 00:00:51.321
Bobby said.

11
00:00:51.341 --> 00:00:54.023
"I heard that, Bobby!"

12
00:00:54.443 --> 00:00:55.584
Chef snapped.

13
00:00:55.604 --> 00:00:59.528
"Sorry, Chef," Bobby said.

14
00:01:00.644 --> 00:01:02.025
"I'll do the first step."

15
00:01:03.847 --> 00:01:05.988
Bobby put a half cup of butter in a pan.

16
00:01:07.650 --> 00:01:08.791
Chef turned on the oven.

17
00:01:11.053 --> 00:01:13.034
He put the pan inside to melt the butter.

18
00:01:13.054 --> 00:01:17.998
"Next we'll coat the chicken in flour," Chef said.

19
00:01:19.159 --> 00:01:22.241
Nina measured two-thirds cup of flour into a bowl.

20
00:01:24.023 --> 00:01:26.765
The kids took turns picking up the chicken with tongs.

21
00:01:28.166 --> 00:01:29.908
They coated each piece with flour.

22
00:01:32.552 --> 00:01:34.993
"Now comes the fun part," Chef said.

23
00:01:36.094 --> 00:01:37.534
"We need cracker crumbs."

24
00:01:39.955 --> 00:01:42.296
He gave each kid a plastic bag of crackers.

25
00:01:42.316 --> 00:01:44.137
"Crush them!"

26
00:01:46.018 --> 00:01:48.439
Nina used a rolling pin to crush the crackers.

27
00:01:50.359 --> 00:01:51.440
Izzie found a mallet.

28
00:01:54.061 --> 00:01:56.622
Bobby pounded his bag on the counter with his fist.

29
00:01:58.603 --> 00:02:00.063
Jason just watched everyone.

30
00:02:00.083 --> 00:02:03.549
"Jason, why aren't you following directions?"

31
00:02:04.089 --> 00:02:04.749
Chef asked.

32
00:02:04.769 --> 00:02:09.811
"I don't feel like cooking today," Jason said.

33
00:02:09.831 --> 00:02:13.013
"But you love cooking!"

34
00:02:13.493 --> 00:02:14.153
Nina said.

35
00:02:14.173 --> 00:02:16.254
"Not anymore."

36
00:02:18.095 --> 00:02:20.456
Jason sighed and handed his bag to Bobby.

37
00:02:23.877 --> 00:02:26.118
The kids poured the cracker crumbs into a bowl.

38
00:02:27.758 --> 00:02:29.059
Izzie looked at the screen.

39
00:02:29.079 --> 00:02:31.180
"We need four eggs.

40
00:02:32.224 --> 00:02:33.064
I'll crack two!"

41
00:02:33.084 --> 00:02:36.525
"I'll crack the other two," Nina said.

42
00:02:42.327 --> 00:02:45.248
Bobby added salt and paprika to the bowl of eggs.

43
00:02:45.268 --> 00:02:50.210
"Jason, add the lemon juice," Chef said.

44
00:02:51.210 --> 00:02:52.150
Jason shrugged.

45
00:02:52.170 --> 00:02:58.092
"Okay." He put four tablespoons of lemon juice in the bowl.

46
00:03:01.996 --> 00:03:03.917
Bobby whisked the ingredients together.

47
00:03:03.937 --> 00:03:08.059
"Now dip the chicken pieces in the egg mixture.

48
00:03:09.040 --> 00:03:11.661
Then coat them in the crumbs," Chef said.

49
00:03:13.662 --> 00:03:15.283
The kids followed his directions.

50
00:03:15.303 --> 00:03:21.046
"We'll bake the pieces for 45 minutes," Chef said.

51
00:03:21.066 --> 00:03:23.728
"We'll turn them over halfway through."

52
00:03:31.372 --> 00:03:32.733
The kids got busy cleaning.

53
00:03:34.114 --> 00:03:36.676
Bobby wiped the counters while Izzie swept the floor.

54
00:03:38.318 --> 00:03:40.359
Jason and Nina washed dishes.

55
00:03:40.379 --> 00:03:44.042
"Jason, why don't you like to cook anymore?"

56
00:03:44.523 --> 00:03:45.183
Chef asked.

57
00:03:45.203 --> 00:03:47.966
"You're an excellent junior chef."

58
00:03:49.247 --> 00:03:50.147
Jason sighed.

59
00:03:50.167 --> 00:03:52.910
"Mom and I cook together all the time.

60
00:03:54.771 --> 00:03:58.194
But when it's just Dad and me, he's always tired after work.

61
00:03:59.315 --> 00:04:00.496
So we get takeout."

62
00:04:02.420 --> 00:04:03.681
Bobby rubbed his stomach.

63
00:04:04.722 --> 00:04:06.524
"Mmm! Takeout!"

64
00:04:06.544 --> 00:04:12.248
"It's good but it's usually not that healthy," Izzie said.

65
00:04:12.268 --> 00:04:17.352
"I wish Dad and I could make meals together," Jason said.

66
00:04:17.372 --> 00:04:21.336
"Have you told your dad you want to cook?"

67
00:04:21.756 --> 00:04:22.577
Nina asked.

68
00:04:23.978 --> 00:04:25.699
"Sure," Jason said.

69
00:04:25.719 --> 00:04:28.641
"But we never have the ingredients I need.

70
00:04:29.842 --> 00:04:31.644
Dad doesn't have time for shopping either."

71
00:04:33.292 --> 00:04:36.896
"When my mom is busy, she has groceries delivered," Izzie said.

72
00:04:36.916 --> 00:04:41.159
"Huh," Jason said, thinking.

73
00:04:43.342 --> 00:04:44.923
Soon the chicken was ready.

74
00:04:46.705 --> 00:04:48.106
Chef placed it on a platter.

75
00:04:51.629 --> 00:04:53.531
He took out some rolls and a salad.

76
00:04:55.993 --> 00:04:58.536
They carried everything to the picnic table outside.

77
00:05:02.228 --> 00:05:03.509
Jason looked at the food.

78
00:05:03.529 --> 00:05:06.151
"I could make this dinner at home.

79
00:05:07.332 --> 00:05:10.794
I'll ask Dad to get groceries delivered, and we'll cook together."

80
00:05:11.915 --> 00:05:13.396
His friends and Chef clapped.

81
00:05:15.257 --> 00:05:16.198
Jason grinned.

82
00:05:16.218 --> 00:05:18.860
"What are we cooking next, Chef?"
